-- Tests for the exceptions group: Chapter 4 (ss 76-95) and Chapter 4A
-- (ss 96-106A) of the Penal Code 1871, and the roll-up in pc-exceptions.l4.
--
-- Expected values come FROM THE SOURCE: each Illustration is cited on the line
-- above its assertion (`-- s 79 illus (b)`); an Explanation applied as a test
-- is cited the same way. Variants that are not Illustrations say which words of
-- the section decide them. A failing assertion here is a finding, not a typo.
--
-- The fixtures spell every field of their record (L4 has no record update), so
-- each lists all leaves with the ones the Illustration establishes set TRUE.
-- (They were expanded from a short template by a script that reads the field
-- lists out of the DECLAREs and rejects a misspelt field; this file is the
-- source of record and may be edited by hand.)
--
-- The POLARITY property (FORK E-1): for every exception, the all-FALSE record -
-- what the charge generator sends when nothing is known - gives FALSE. That is
-- Evidence Act 1893 s 107's "the court is to presume the absence of such
-- circumstances", asserted once per exported ladder in the last section.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pc-domain`
IMPORT `pc-general`
IMPORT `pc-exceptions-general`
IMPORT `pc-exceptions-private-defence`
IMPORT `pc-exceptions`

