§§ `s 76`

-- s 76 illus (a): a soldier fires on a mob by the order of his superior
-- officer, in conformity with the commands of the law. No offence.
@@FIX `a soldier firing on a mob by lawful order` : Bound or Justified by Law Facts
bound by law
@@END
#ASSERT `exception under s 76` `a soldier firing on a mob by lawful order`

-- s 76 illus (b): A forcefully seizes Z, who is stabbing Y to death on a
-- public road, to detain him for the police, under the power the law gives to
